# Requires PowerShell 7.3+ (pwsh); not compatible with Windows PowerShell 5.1.
<#
Workflow.psm1

Module for AWS server workflow for DEER simulation and post-processing

Function execution order:

Github workflow (run_deer_simulations.yml)
|
| Checkout measure repository from given model_ref, determine commit_sha
| aws ec2 start-instance ...
| aws ssm send-command ...
V
BootstrapSimulation.ps1
|
| Download and extract the deer-cloud-compute-setup package (WorkflowPackageS3Key) frozen for this run
| Import Workflow.psm1 from the extracted package
V
Invoke-DEERWorkflowController (RequestedSteps)
|
+-- Generate manifest
+-- Create working directory
|
+-- Initialize-DEERRepository
|   +-- Clone repository
|   +-- Checkout specified commit
|   +-- Initialize submodules/helper repositories
|   \-- (future enhancement) Resume workflow stored in S3 on a new virtual machine
|
+-- Invoke-WorkflowStep(StepName1)
|     |
|     +-- start transcript
|     |
|     +-- Invoke-PackageQc / Invoke-Compose / Invoke-Simulate ...
|     |     |
|     |     +-- Modelkit rake / Python / ...
|     |     +-- Capture command output to step-command.log file
|     |     \-- Sync large files to S3
|     |
|     +-- Gather command line exit value and status into step-status.json
|     \-- upload artifacts to S3 (transcript, step-status.json, output files, metrics)
|
+-- Update manifest file
|
+-- Repeat (iterate over new workflow step) 
+-- Generate workflow-summary.md
+-- Upload workflow-level artifacts to S3
|     +-- run-manifest.json
|     +-- workflow-summary.json
|     \-- controller transcript


The package-qc step discovers the scenarios and generates the scenario inventory
that will be used by subsequent compose and simulate steps.

Invoke-PackageQc
|
+-- measure-qc.json
+-- measure-qc.md
\-- scenario-index.json

The compose step iterates over the scenario inventory discovered at the package-qc step.
Each simulate-N matrix job runs one scenario on its own instance.

Invoke-Compose
|
+-- Read scenario-index.json
+-- Loop through scenarios
\-- modelkit rake compose

Github workflow resumes after the workflow controller completes the requested steps.

AWS SSM wait for completion
| "done"
V
Github worklow
|
+-- Download step-status.json, summary.md, metrics from S3
+-- Download review files from S3
+-- Upload artifacts to Github artifacts
\-- Display step summary, artifacts, and links to CloudWatch logs and S3 directory in browser


## Workflow output Files

run-manifest.json
(Intent of the workflow run attempt)
|
V
step-status.json
(step evidence, including exit codes, stdout/stderr, and generated artifacts)
|
V
workflow-summary.json
(aggregated facts, including overall workflow status, step summaries, and key metrics)
|
V
summary.md
(GitHub presentation, including a human-readable summary of the workflow run)

Terminology:
- RunId: Unique identifier for the workflow run, e.g. "1234567890". Usually generated by Github Actions.
- RunAttempt: Attempt number for the current workflow run, e.g. "1". Generated by Github Actions.
- S3Bucket: S3 bucket name used for storing artifacts. Configured in the workflow or via environment variables.
- StepName: Name of the current workflow step (e.g., package-qc, compose, simulate). Defined by the workflow.
- WorkingDirectory: Local working directory for the step. Typically set by the workflow.
- OutputDirectory: Directory where step artifacts are stored. Typically within the working directory.
- ManifestPath: Path to the manifest file. Usually located in the working directory.
- Command: Script block representing the actual workload. Provided by the workflow step definition.
- RequiredInputs: Optional validation for required inputs. Specified in the workflow step definition.
- RequiredOutputs: Optional validation for required outputs. Specified in the workflow step definition.
- PlannedSteps = all steps that belong to this workflow (even if not requested to run yet)
- RequestedSteps = the step(s) being executed right now

#>

# TODO: consider using DVC package to manage syncing data to S3
# https://doc.dvc.org/start

# Global variable to define the expected inputs and outputs for each step in the workflow.
$WorkflowStepDefinitions = @{
    
    "package-qc" = @{
        Resources = @(
        "repository checkout",
        "measure directory"
        )
        Outputs = @(
        "measure-qc.json",
        "measure-qc.md",
        "scenario-index.json"
        )
    }
    "compose" = @{
